The Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA) is a vital tool in this community, specifically designed for the early detection of malnutrition in elderly individuals. It is widely recognized for its high sensitivity and is recommended by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) for use in both institutional and outpatient settings. The MNA evaluates various aspects of nutritional status and is linked to criteria of frailty, making it essential for comprehensive geriatric assessments. Its integration into healthcare practices underscores its significance in identifying at-risk individuals and facilitating timely interventions [Data: Entities (560); Relationships (2924, 3915, 3914)].

