Anthropometric measurements are essential for monitoring the growth and nutritional status of children. These measurements help identify potential growth issues early, allowing for timely interventions. Regular assessments can track changes in body composition and ensure that children are meeting their growth milestones. This proactive approach is crucial in preventing long-term health consequences associated with malnutrition. [Data: Relationships (4163)]

