Children exhibit a notable capacity for intestinal adaptation, which is particularly important for their growth and health, especially after surgical interventions. This adaptability allows children to adjust to changes in their diet and nutrient absorption, making it essential for healthcare providers to consider this factor when planning nutritional regimens. Understanding the mechanisms of intestinal adaptation can help in developing effective dietary strategies for children recovering from surgeries or facing nutritional challenges. [Data: Relationships (19154)]# Nutritional Evaluation and Health Management

