## Celiac disease as a serious health condition

Celiac disease is an autoimmune disorder that can lead to severe health complications if not managed properly. It is triggered by the ingestion of gluten, which damages the small intestine and can result in malabsorption of essential nutrients. This condition necessitates a strict gluten-free diet to prevent further complications, highlighting the importance of awareness and education about the disease. The interconnectedness of various entities in this community underscores the need for comprehensive management strategies for affected individuals. [Data: Entities (9729); Relationships (16904, 17888, 16809)]

