Finland is noted for having a high prevalence of congenital lactase deficiency, with most cases reported in the Finnish population. This geographical concentration highlights the importance of genetic factors in the expression of lactase deficiency and suggests a need for targeted health interventions in these populations. Understanding the demographic factors associated with lactase deficiency can inform public health strategies. [Data: Entities (9726); Relationships (17886)]# Glycogen Storage Disease Type III and Research Community

