Excessive consumption of certain ingredients can contribute to chronic diarrhea, particularly in sensitive individuals. This highlights the need for dietary assessments in patients experiencing chronic diarrhea, as dietary modifications may alleviate symptoms. Understanding the dietary triggers is essential for comprehensive management and can significantly improve patient outcomes. [Data: Entities (12148), Relationships (15191)]

