Systemic diseases and intestinal disorders are significant contributors to chronic diarrhea. Conditions such as vasculitis and other systemic diseases can affect gastrointestinal function, leading to diarrhea. Recognizing the broader implications of systemic health on gastrointestinal symptoms is crucial for holistic patient care. [Data: Entities (12142, 12146), Relationships (15184, 15189)]# Higado and Hereditary Fructose Intolerance Community

