The ALDOB gene is critical for the metabolism of fructose, and mutations in this gene lead to hereditary fructose intolerance. Understanding the genetic basis of this condition is essential for diagnosis and management. The relationship between the ALDOB gene and the liver's metabolic functions highlights the interconnectedness of genetics and organ health in managing metabolic disorders. [Data: Entities (9600), Relationships (17811, 15194)]# Fructose and Dietary Intolerances Community

