Sorbitol is often consumed alongside fructose in various food products, which can lead to increased symptoms of intolerance in sensitive individuals. The combined effects of these sugars can complicate dietary management for those with intolerances, making it essential for consumers to read labels carefully and understand the potential interactions between these ingredients [Data: Relationships (17683, 17685)].# Dietary Intolerances and Related Conditions

