## Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) as a central condition

Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) is a prevalent gastrointestinal disorder that significantly impacts individuals' quality of life. It is characterized by symptoms such as cramping, abdominal pain, and alterations in bowel habits, which can lead to misdiagnosis with other conditions like celiac disease and lactose intolerance. The complexity of IBS is further compounded by its relationship with food intolerances, particularly fructose malabsorption, which can exacerbate symptoms. This interrelation highlights the need for careful diagnosis and management strategies to alleviate the burden on affected individuals [Data: Entities (9723); Relationships (17881, 17879, 17880, 17884, 17883, +more)].

