## Sorbitol's impact on dietary intolerances

Sorbitol, a sugar alcohol commonly found in various food products, poses a significant risk for individuals with dietary intolerances, particularly those with hereditary fructose intolerance and IBS. The consumption of sorbitol can lead to osmotic diarrhea and exacerbate gastrointestinal symptoms in sensitive individuals. Its presence in baked goods and diabetic products further complicates dietary management, as these items may not be easily identifiable sources of sorbitol. Understanding the implications of sorbitol consumption is essential for individuals managing these conditions [Data: Entities (9475); Relationships (17681, 17686, 17688, +more)].

