## Malabsorci√≥n de Fructosa and its implications

Malabsorci√≥n de fructosa is a significant condition characterized by the inability to absorb fructose, leading to symptoms such as diarrhea and abdominal pain. This condition is closely linked to dietary management, as certain foods can exacerbate symptoms. The relationships show that proper nutrition is essential in managing this condition, indicating a need for dietary interventions to prevent complications [Data: Entities (9765), Relationships (753, 4207, 3853)].

