## Diabetic Ketoacidosis as a severe complication

Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) is a severe metabolic complication of diabetes mellitus characterized by hyperglycemia, hyperketonemia, and metabolic acidosis. It requires urgent medical intervention due to its serious nature, as it can lead to a dangerous buildup of acids in the bloodstream. The condition is often precipitated by poorly managed diabetes, highlighting the importance of effective diabetes management to prevent DKA. [Data: Entities (4184); Relationships (1503, 9706, 8809, 13324, 8826, +more)]

