Medications such as angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors (IECA) and statins are recommended for managing complications associated with glucogenosis. These treatments are essential for addressing issues like microalbuminuria and dyslipidemia, which can arise in patients with glycogen storage diseases. The integration of pharmacological interventions into patient care is vital for optimizing health outcomes and managing the multifaceted nature of these disorders. [Data: Entities (10737, 13568); Relationships (18340, 14966)]# Diabetes 2 Research Community

