## Ictus as a major health concern in Spain

Ictus is recognized as a leading health issue in Spain, being the second leading cause of death in the population. This condition predominantly affects the elderly and women, necessitating urgent attention to prevention and management strategies. The high prevalence of ictus underscores the need for effective healthcare interventions to address the associated complications, such as dysphagia and dehydration, which can further complicate recovery. [Data: Entities (152); Relationships (1868)]

