## The interrelation of dehydration and dysphagia

Dehydration is a significant risk for patients with dysphagia, as their inability to swallow liquids effectively can lead to inadequate fluid intake. This relationship highlights the importance of monitoring fluid consumption in vulnerable populations, particularly those recovering from an ictus. Addressing dehydration is essential to prevent further health complications, including increased mortality rates. [Data: Entities (190); Relationships (157, 2000)]

