Rheology, the study of flow and deformation of materials, is vital for understanding how thickeners function. It provides insights into the properties of food boluses and the behavior of liquids, which is essential for developing effective thickeners for dysphagia patients. By studying the flow characteristics of thickened liquids, rheology helps in formulating products that meet the dietary needs of individuals with swallowing difficulties. This connection between rheology and thickeners highlights the importance of scientific research in improving food safety and nutrition for vulnerable populations [Data: Entities (762); Relationships (302, 5051)].

