The community is centered around the European Society for Swallowing Disorders (ESSD) and the International Dysphagia Diet Standardisation Initiative (IDDSI), both of which are dedicated to improving the understanding and management of swallowing disorders, particularly dysphagia. The ESSD plays a crucial role in advancing research and education, while the IDDSI focuses on standardizing dietary practices for affected individuals.

## ESSD's pivotal role in dysphagia research and education

The European Society for Swallowing Disorders (ESSD) is a key entity in the community, dedicated to advancing research and education concerning swallowing disorders, particularly dysphagia. The organization has been instrumental in establishing guidelines and standards for the diagnosis and treatment of these disorders, ensuring that healthcare professionals are equipped with the most current practices. In 2012, the ESSD hosted a significant meeting that led to the initiation of the International Dysphagia Diet Standardisation Initiative (IDDSI), highlighting its influence in the field. This foundational role underscores the ESSD's importance in shaping the landscape of dysphagia management and education [Data: Entities (389); Relationships (2158, 3004)].

