The EAT-10 is a validated self-assessment questionnaire that plays a crucial role in evaluating swallowing problems, specifically dysphagia. It is widely recognized in clinical settings for its effectiveness in identifying dysphagia symptoms, making it an essential tool for healthcare professionals. The EAT-10 is utilized in various hospital wards, ensuring that patients at risk of dysphagia are properly assessed and managed. Its availability in multiple languages, including Spanish, enhances its accessibility and usability in diverse patient populations [Data: Entities (336); Relationships (282, 2450, 2453, 2457, 2444, +more)].

