MEN2A, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia Type 2A, is a significant genetic disorder characterized by mutations in the RET proto-oncogene. This condition poses a high risk for developing medullary thyroid carcinoma, pheochromocytomas, and hyperparathyroidism, making it essential for affected individuals to receive early diagnosis and preventive treatment. The prevalence of these tumors in MEN2A patients underscores the importance of genetic screening and regular monitoring to mitigate health risks. [Data: Entities (4733); Relationships (14019, 14024, 14030)]

