Total thyroidectomy is a surgical procedure recommended for patients with MEN2A to prevent the development of medullary thyroid carcinoma. This intervention is critical for managing the risks associated with RET mutations, particularly in patients diagnosed with thyroid cancer. The procedure involves the complete removal of the thyroid gland, which is essential for patients with specific RET mutations to avoid malignant transformations. [Data: Entities (4758); Relationships (14030)]

