MIBG is a crucial radiopharmaceutical used for both the diagnosis and treatment of pheochromocytomas, which are tumors that secrete catecholamines. Its high affinity for chromaffin cells makes it an essential tool in imaging, allowing for the detection of these tumors. MIBG provides valuable anatomical and functional information, enhancing the understanding and management of conditions associated with catecholamine-secreting tumors. This is supported by its relationship with pheochromocytoma, where MIBG is utilized diagnostically and therapeutically due to its effectiveness in targeting these specific tumors [Data: Entities (5168); Relationships (11937, 13330)].

