TAC is commonly used as the first imaging technique to locate tumors before MIBG imaging is performed. This sequential approach enhances the diagnostic process, allowing for more accurate localization of pheochromocytomas. The relationship between TAC and MIBG illustrates the importance of using multiple imaging modalities to improve patient outcomes in the diagnosis and treatment of catecholamine-secreting tumors [Data: Relationships (12792)].

