Vancomicina is a broad-spectrum antibiotic that has been shown to increase the abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila in rodents. This relationship highlights the potential of Vancomicina not only in treating infections but also in influencing gut health. The increase in Akkermansia muciniphila following Vancomicina treatment suggests that antibiotics can have complex effects on gut microbiota, which may lead to improved metabolic health outcomes. This is particularly relevant in the context of obesity and diabetes, where gut microbiota composition plays a crucial role. [Data: Entities (6847, 9015); Relationships (16098)]

