The NOD mouse is a widely used model in diabetes research, particularly for studying autoimmune diabetes. This model allows researchers to investigate the mechanisms underlying diabetes development and progression, providing valuable insights that can inform treatment strategies. The relationship between the NOD mouse and other entities, such as Diabetologia, highlights its importance in the research landscape, as studies published in the journal often utilize this model to explore various aspects of diabetes. [Data: Entities (9140), Relationships (17387, 16533)]

