The BODE index is a multidimensional grading system that plays a crucial role in assessing the severity of EPOC. It incorporates various factors such as BMI, airway obstruction, dyspnea, and exercise capacity, making it a comprehensive tool for predicting mortality and outcomes in EPOC patients. The BODE index's emphasis on nutritional status highlights its importance in the overall management of EPOC, as poor nutrition can significantly impact patient health and recovery. [Data: Entities (13010); Relationships (4099, 19329)]

