The management of medications is crucial for patient care, especially for those with specific health conditions. Medications can significantly influence a patient's nutritional status, making it essential to evaluate their intake during health assessments. For instance, the number of medications a patient takes can directly affect their overall health and nutritional needs, particularly in the context of the Mini Nutritional Assessment. This highlights the importance of careful medication management to ensure optimal health outcomes. [Data: Entities (576); Relationships (3038, 4016, 4017)]

