## Insulina Glargina as a cornerstone of diabetes management

Insulina Glargina is a long-acting insulin that plays a vital role in managing blood sugar levels for patients with diabetes, particularly those with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. It is administered at night to maintain steady insulin levels, which is crucial for effective diabetes management. The significance of Insulina Glargina is underscored by its use in various contexts, including post-surgery and nutritional therapy, making it a versatile option for patients. Its relationship with diabetes management is further emphasized by its frequent prescription and monitoring in patients, indicating its importance in treatment regimens [Data: Entities (4328); Relationships (5741, 13494, 13504, 13503, 13505, +more)].

