Regular monitoring of glucemias, or blood sugar levels, is essential for patients with diabetes, particularly those undergoing insulin therapy. This practice allows for timely adjustments to insulin dosages and treatment plans, ensuring effective management of blood glucose levels. In patients with Alzheimer's disease, monitoring glucemias becomes even more critical, as it directly impacts their overall health and treatment outcomes. The relationship between glucemias and insulin treatments highlights the importance of continuous assessment in diabetes care [Data: Entities (6849); Relationships (3275, 13504, +more)].

