Hematopoietic cell transplantation is a vital medical procedure used to treat various hematological diseases, including certain cancers. This procedure is considered potentially curative and involves the transfer of hematopoietic stem cells, which can restore blood function. The complexity of this treatment necessitates comprehensive care, including high doses of chemotherapy and nutritional support, making it a significant focus within the medical community. [Data: Entities (13735), Relationships (19646, 4418)]

