The HLA system is associated with genetic predispositions to autoimmune diseases, particularly Type 1 Diabetes. Specific haplotypes, such as DR3-DQ2 and DR4-DQ8, are linked to increased susceptibility to this condition. Understanding these genetic factors is vital for predicting disease risk and tailoring preventive strategies for at-risk individuals. The relationship between HLA haplotypes and autoimmune diseases emphasizes the importance of genetic screening in clinical practice. [Data: Entities (4065, 4066); Relationships (9610, 9611, 13042)]

