Growth hormone is utilized in the treatment of patients with severe burns, as it aids in reducing healing time and associated costs. This therapeutic application highlights the hormone's importance in recovery processes and its potential to improve patient outcomes in critical care settings. The relationship between growth hormone and burn patients emphasizes its role in enhancing healing and recovery. [Data: Relationships (9518)]

