Hypophosphatemia, characterized by low serum phosphorus levels, is a common complication in patients with chronic kidney disease. This condition can arise from various factors, including dietary imbalances and the effects of treatments such as parenteral nutrition. The management of phosphorus levels is crucial for CKD patients to avoid severe health issues [Data: Entities (1911); Relationships (7822, 7820)].

