Protein-Energy Wasting (PEW) is a serious syndrome affecting patients with chronic kidney disease, characterized by the loss of body protein mass and energy reserves. This condition can lead to malnutrition, which significantly impacts patient outcomes and quality of life. The relationship between chronic kidney disease and PEW is well-documented, indicating that the management of nutritional status is crucial for these patients. [Data: Entities (10066); Relationships (9157)]

