This community focuses on the interrelated entities of PCR, nutritional screening, and nutritional risk, which are crucial in evaluating the health status of patients, particularly in surgical contexts. The relationships among these entities highlight the importance of assessing inflammation and nutritional needs to prevent malnutrition and related complications.

## PCR as a key inflammatory marker

PCR, or C-reactive protein, is a significant marker of inflammation that plays a crucial role in evaluating the health status of patients, particularly in surgical contexts. Elevated levels of PCR can indicate a heightened inflammatory response, which may suggest nutritional risk among surgical patients. This makes PCR an essential tool in clinical settings for monitoring patient health and guiding treatment decisions. [Data: Entities (3252), Relationships (9097, 11429)]

