Nutritional risk refers to the potential for malnutrition and is assessed based on various criteria, including serum albumin levels and body mass index (BMI). The assessment of nutritional risk is essential before surgical procedures to determine the need for nutritional support. This relationship highlights the interconnectedness of nutritional risk with both PCR levels and nutritional screening processes. [Data: Entities (3241), Relationships (11415, 11418)]

