Metoclopramida is a medication that plays a significant role in enhancing enteral nutrition by promoting gastric emptying and alleviating nausea. It is particularly effective in oncology patients who often experience nausea that can hinder their nutritional intake. The administration of Metoclopramida is essential in critical care settings, where it is used to manage symptoms and improve the overall tolerance of enteral nutrition. However, it is important to note that Metoclopramida may cause diarrhea, which can complicate the nutritional management of patients. [Data: Entities (2282); Relationships (3101, 2806, 9491)]

