Nutritional support is critical for managing patients with sepsis, as their nutritional needs are often significantly altered due to the condition. While nutritional support can increase the risk of sepsis in vulnerable populations, it is also essential for recovery. Specific interventions, such as amino acid supplementation, may be beneficial in addressing the heightened metabolic stress experienced by patients suffering from sepsis. This dual role underscores the complexity of nutritional management in this context. [Data: Relationships (6753, 6831, 6833)]

